    "https://www.haverford.edu/provost/news/mellon-post-doctoral-fellow-1": {
      "title": "Mellon Post-Doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Mellon Post-Doctoral Fellow | Haverford College Skip to main content Haverford College Logo, homepage Haverford College Search Menu Log In Log in HC Gmail Moodle Bionic Human Resources Workday Mellon Post-Doctoral Fellow Haverford College invites applications for a two-year, full-time Postdoctoral Fellowship to begin Fall 2027. The John B. Hurford ’60 Center for the Arts and Humanities at Haverford College invites applications for a two-year, full-time Mellon Postdoctoral Fellowship to begin Fall 2027. We seek a humanistic scholar of sound studies whose work focuses on the cultural history of listening practices. Topics of particular interest include: modes of attention; cultural memory; post-secularity; disability; (un)disciplining the ear; listening as ethical and/or activist practice; professional (e.g. psychoanalytic, medical, juridical) practices of listening. Candidates’ work should be fundamentally grounded in sound studies but may also draw from a range of fields in the humanities, including history, literary studies, religious studies, performance studies, gender and sexuality studies, disability studies, Indigenous studies, and area studies (Asian, African, Latin American, and/or American Studies). During the first year of the program, the Mellon Postdoctoral Fellow will participate in the faculty seminar \"Acts of Listening\" led by Professor Gustavus Stadler (English), which will bring together faculty from a variety of fields. Drawing from over a century of writing in various modalities and disciplines, it explores practices of audition in diverse cultural and historical contexts, across diverse aural phenomena (music, speech, noise, sounds of bodies, sounds of ritual, and more) in diverse spaces (aesthetic, political, therapeutic, pedagogical, and more). The seminar will explore such questions as: How does listening shape cultural and individual memory? What institutions impact the ways we listen? Is aural attention different from other forms of attention? Is it productive to think in terms of an ethics of listening? What is the relationship between listening and divinity? Listening and intimacy/confession? Is there a post–secular way to listen? During each of their four semesters at Haverford College, the Fellow will teach one course at the intermediate/advanced level and engage a diverse student body. The postdoctoral fellow will deliver a lecture in the spring semester of the first year and will pursue mentorship opportunities in the second year to support their professional growth. While the Fellow is under no obligation to organize any additional activities – they are to focus on their own writing and protect their time – we encourage the Fellow to make use of our proximity to Philadelphia and engage with artists, activists, and intellectuals in the Greater Philadelphia area. The fellow will have an office in the interdisciplinary VCAM (Visual Culture Arts and Media) building, the College's 24/7 creative hub for students, faculty, staff, and the wider community. Home to Haverford's Visual Studies Program, the Haverford Innovations Program, and the John B. Hurford ’60 Center for the Arts and Humanities, VCAM features a host of flexible spaces for teaching and making, including a Film/Media Edit Studio, Maker Arts Space, two Create Spaces, Artist Residency Studio, Object Study/Media Production Classroom, and exhibitions spaces. Candidates who have earned their Ph.D. no earlier than 2022 and will have completed all requirements for the Ph.D. by May 1, 2027, are eligible to apply. Applicants must submit the following via Interfolio ( https://apply.interfolio.com/195269 ) by 11:59 p.m. ET on January 8, 2027 : A cover letter A C.V. A research statement [one page] A syllabus for an advanced undergraduate seminar on a topic of your own choosing. Candidates who advance to the second round will be asked to submit a writing sample and two recommendation letters. These candidates will be contacted directly by email with instructions for submitting the additional materials. Questions about the position can be directed to Kelly Jung, at hjung1@haverford.edu . For technical questions about Interfolio, please contact Interfolio directly at 1-877-997-8807 or help@interfolio.com . Haverford College is a leading liberal arts college located 9 miles from the center of Philadelphia. The idyllic residential campus is home to over 1,400 exceptional undergraduate students who are motivated by their deep intellectual curiosity, respectfully collaborative spirit, and commitment to improving the world around them. The diverse neighborhoods comprising the greater Philadelphia area are home to many cultural icons and recreational spaces, with direct public transportation access from Haverford’s campus and excellent access to many cities on the East Coast. The concentration of higher education institutions in the region provides excellent opportunities for facilitating professional connections. Haverford College strives to maintain an equitable, accessible, and welcoming environment where staff, faculty and students of all backgrounds, perspectives, abilities, and experience can work, learn, and thrive. Haverford College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate based on race, ethnicity, religion, gender identity, sexual orientation, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other identity or characteristic protected by law. Haverford College recognizes that we live and work on Lenape land. Antonis Asprakis Coordinator for Faculty Hiring and Programs × Antonis Asprakis Coordinator for Faculty Hiring and Programs Published October 8, 2026 Share Share on Facebook Share this on Twitter/X Share this via email Copy Link Share Related Stories Image Inside the Search for Brian T. Edwards Built Different: Anna Kotler '91 and O'ts Cookies Image Court is in Session Haverford Welcomes Nine New Faculty Members Founded 1833 370 Lancaster Avenue, Haverford, PA 19041 (610) 896-1000 Come Say Hello Directions Visit Campus Campus Map Get to Know Us About Haverford Facts & Statistics Land Acknowledgment Join Our Community Job Openings Faculty Positions Non-discrimination Policy Get Social with Haverford Instagram Facebook Youtube Linked In © 2026 Haverford College. All Rights Reserved. Made with love by Black Squirrels. Back to Top Welcome, friend. Hit enter to Search all of Haverford for Black Squirrel Search Suggestions * * We have a very tiny magic 8 ball. Close search overlay Quick Links Quick Access Make a Gift Main menu About Academics Admission & Aid Campus Life Headlines Events Contacts Information for: Prospective Students Current Students Faculty & Staff Family & Friends Alumni - Choose - Prospective Students Current Students Faculty & Staff Family & Friends Alumni Admission Menu Why Haverford? Giving Join Mailing List Get Social with Haverford Instagram Facebook Youtube Linked In But wait, there's more! Athletics Library Close search overlay"
    },
    "https://www.haverford.edu/provost/news/tenure-track-assistant-professor-health-studies": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Health Studies",
      "description": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Health Studies | Haverford College Skip to main content Haverford College Logo, homepage Haverford College Search Menu Log In Log in HC Gmail Moodle Bionic Human Resources Workday Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Health Studies Haverford College invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Health Studies, to begin Fall semester of 2027. We seek to make an appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor, in the health humanities or critical social sciences of health, including but not limited to medical anthropology and the history of medicine. Candidates in closely-related interdisciplinary fields (for example, gender studies, science and technology studies, comparative literature, ethnic studies, area studies, etc.) are also encouraged to apply if their training, research, and teaching competences align with Health Studies. We invite applications from scholars working on a wide range of topics, including infectious disease, mental health, sexual and reproductive health, non-communicable disease, environmental health, disability, cancer, substance use, medical education, the healing professions, health systems and bureaucracies, political economy of health, therapeutics and medical technologies, among others. We are especially interested in scholars who study health, illness, or health systems using ethnographic, archival, or other qualitative approaches; work that combines these approaches with spatial or visual methods is also welcome. The geographic area of focus is open, though candidates working in the Global South or on global health are strongly encouraged to apply. The record of research and teaching should demonstrate a commitment to interdisciplinarity and critical inquiry, facility with relevant social theory, and attention to intersections between race, racism, and racialization; gender, gender identity, and sexuality; economic inequality and social stratification; disability and difference; linguistic, cultural, and religious diversity; and/or nationality, citizenship, migration, and belonging. Qualifications Candidates should hold an earned doctorate in a humanities or social science discipline, or a closely-related interdisciplinary field, to be completed by the time of appointment. We seek scholars who can teach and mentor undergraduate students with a range of academic interests, experiences, and backgrounds. Candidates must be able to teach Introduction to Health Studies, an intermediate survey course in their subfield, and advanced undergraduate seminars in their areas of expertise. Application Instructions Applicants must submit the following via Interfolio ( https://apply.interfolio.com/193325 ), addressing the scholarly qualifications identified above: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Research statement (2-3 pages) Teaching statement that conveys the applicant’s pedagogical approaches, mentorship experience, and efforts to foster an inclusive academic environment through concrete examples from their courses and teaching praxis (2 pages). A writing sample (e.g., an article or book chapter) Names and contact information for three references. Three confidential letters of recommendation will be solicited only for candidates who are selected for Zoom interviews. All application materials must be submitted by 11:59pm (ET) on October 23, 2026 via Interfolio. Questions about the position can be directed to: hc-healthstudiessearch@haverford.edu . For technical questions about Interfolio, please contact Interfolio directly at 1-877-997-8807 or help@interfolio.com . For more information about Haverford and this position, please see here: https://www.haverford.edu/provost/available-positions/tenure-track-search-health-studies Haverford College strives to maintain an equitable, accessible, and welcoming environment where staff, faculty and students of all backgrounds, perspectives, abilities, and experience can work, learn, and thrive. Haverford College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate based on race, ethnicity, religion, gender identity, sexual orientation, national origin or ancestry, age, marital status, disability, veteran status, or any other identity or characteristic protected by law. Haverford College recognizes that we live and work on Lenape land. Antonis Asprakis Coordinator for Faculty Hiring and Programs × Antonis Asprakis Coordinator for Faculty Hiring and Programs Published September 10, 2026 Share Share on Facebook Share this on Twitter/X Share this via email Copy Link Share Related Stories Image Inside the Search for Brian T. Edwards Built Different: Anna Kotler '91 and O'ts Cookies Image Court is in Session Haverford Welcomes Nine New Faculty Members Founded 1833 370 Lancaster Avenue, Haverford, PA 19041 (610) 896-1000 Come Say Hello Directions Visit Campus Campus Map Get to Know Us About Haverford Facts & Statistics Land Acknowledgment Join Our Community Job Openings Faculty Positions Non-discrimination Policy Get Social with Haverford Instagram Facebook Youtube Linked In © 2026 Haverford College. All Rights Reserved. Made with love by Black Squirrels. Back to Top Welcome, friend. Hit enter to Search all of Haverford for Black Squirrel Search Suggestions * * We have a very tiny magic 8 ball. Close search overlay Quick Links Quick Access Make a Gift Main menu About Academics Admission & Aid Campus Life Headlines Events Contacts Information for: Prospective Students Current Students Faculty & Staff Family & Friends Alumni - Choose - Prospective Students Current Students Faculty & Staff Family & Friends Alumni Admission Menu Why Haverford? Giving Join Mailing List Get Social with Haverford Instagram Facebook Youtube Linked In But wait, there's more! Athletics Library Close search overlay"
